   "page": 5,
   "mark": "5",
   "text": "ItshouldbenotedthattheHastings-McLeodsolutionisveryunstable;indeed,asmallchangeinthe pre-exponential numerical factor in the normalization condition (3.7) yields a completely diﬀerent type of behavior of u(x) for negative x, including the appearance of singularities (e.g. see again [FIKN] ). Herein lies the importance of the knowledge of the behavior (3.9) in order to adjust the numerical procedure appropriately. Said diﬀerently, knowledge of the connection formulae makes it possible to transform an unstable ODE initial value problem into a stable ODE boundary value problem.",
